From 15916fe9bf162fe935af39f5a11592843e3d3682 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:48:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ActiveAE: an output that is not there is replaced before its
 formats are asked

Every new stream, reconfiguration and retry loads the audio settings again
(LoadSettings()), and took again a configured output that the engine did
not list in this start. Kodi validates the settings when it starts and
after every change of the outputs (ValidateOutputDevices()), but only for
the next configuration: each stream then tried to open the output that is
not there, the sink fell back to the first output of the list (or the one
with the display in its place), and everything decided before that was
asked of the configured output, whose formats are not known. SupportsRaw()
said no, so nothing passed through, and the channels of PCM were not
limited to what the display takes.

A session of 2026-10-17 shows it on the PC of the user: the setting named
the HDMI output of the integrated graphics, the PC was started with the
NVIDIA graphics only, and with displays on three NVIDIA outputs the
setting is not followed to one of them (the choice stays with the user).
In nine streams Dolby TrueHD and Dolby Digital were decoded to PCM, each
one tried to open "hdmi:CARD=HDMI,DEV=0" and fell back to the TV; after
the output was chosen again in the settings, TrueHD passed through.

The output in place of one that is not there is now chosen in
LoadSettings(), after FollowDisplay(): the output that Kodi validates it
to when Kodi takes it for the same device (the same driver and card name,
a card renamed), or else the output that the sink fell back to
(CActiveAESink::FallbackOutput(), the choice of OpenSink()). Where the
streams go is not changed, the same output is now the one whose formats
are asked, and no stream tries to open an output that is not there. The
decision is INTERNAL::OutputForSetting(), with host tests. The engine logs
the output it uses in its place once, without debugging.

A change of the count of outputs (PulseAudio, PipeWire) used to be
decided with the device of the last LoadSettings(); it is now decided
with what the settings give with the outputs listed again
(ResolveOutput(), what FollowDisplay() gives without logging or keeping
anything), so that a configured output that comes back (Bluetooth
headphones turned on during a video) is taken again, and an output in
place of one that stays away is not reopened.

The setting is never written: when the output is listed again (every
change of the outputs lists them again), it is used again. Kodi used to
save, when it started, the validated output with the same card name in
the setting; the device in use is now that output already, so the
setting stays as the user chose it. Limit: an output that the engine
cannot list but could open (an ALSA name written by hand in the
settings file, or an output that another program held while the outputs
were listed) is no longer tried again before the next change of the
outputs.
---
